STEP 8 — Basic Field Error

The New Patient form can display a validation message
directly below a field.

Example:

Mobile
[ abc123 ]
Mobile number must contain exactly 10 digits.

The HTML field has a small <small> element for the error.

JavaScript finds that element using:

document.getElementById("mobileError")

and changes:

textContent

This is a basic DOM operation.

We are intentionally only demonstrating this pattern
for the mobile field instead of creating a large
validation UI system.

The validation rule itself remains in validation.js.

patient-form.js decides when to display the message.

This keeps responsibilities separate.


STEP 9 — Success vs Error Message

Error messages use:

error-message

Success messages use:

success-message

CSS controls how each class looks.

JavaScript changes the class depending on the result.

This is a simple example of:

JavaScript
    ↓
changes CSS class
    ↓
CSS changes appearance